# zec-bounties-backend: environment variables

Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values for your machine:

```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

Every variable below is read by the backend code. Variables marked
**optional for local dev** can be left as-is (or empty) when you only want
to run the API + frontend locally; the features that need them
(payments, email, push notifications, GitHub login) will be unavailable
or degraded, but the server still starts.

```env
# Port the API listens on. Optional for local dev (defaults to 9000).
# Must match the frontend's dev backendUrl (zec-bounties-frontend/lib/configENV.ts).
PORT=9000

# PostgreSQL connection string used by Prisma. Required.
# Example: postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/zec_bounties
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/zec_bounties"

# Secret used to sign/verify auth JWTs. Required for login to work.
JWT_SECRET=<redacted>

# Public origin of the frontend, used for CORS. Optional for local dev
# (defaults to http://localhost:3000).
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Path to the zingo-cli binary, used to send ZEC payouts.
# Optional for local dev (payment features only).
ZINGO_CLI=/path/to/zingo-cli

# Pinata JWT for pinning files to IPFS. Optional for local dev.
PINATA_JWT=your_pinata_jwt

# Pinata gateway base URL for reading IPFS content. Optional for local dev.
PINATA_GATEWAY=https://gateway.pinata.cloud

# SMTP credentials for outgoing email. Optional for local dev.
SMTP_USER=you@example.com
SMTP_PASS=smtp_password

# In non-production, all outgoing email is redirected to this address
# instead of the real recipient. Optional for local dev.
DEV_EMAIL_FALLBACK=dev@example.com

# Web Push (VAPID) keys and contact email for push notifications.
# Optional for local dev.
VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=your_vapid_public_key
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=your_vapid_private_key
VAPID_EMAIL=mailto:you@example.com

# Redis connection string, used for caching/queues.
# Optional for local dev (defaults to redis://localhost:6379).
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379

# Zcash node RPC credentials, used for on-chain payment calls.
# Optional for local dev (payment features only; needs Zebrad/Zaino running).
ZCASH_RPC_USER=rpcuser
ZCASH_RPC_PASS=rpcpassword
ZCASH_RPC_URL=http://localhost:8232

# GitHub OAuth app credentials, used for "Login with GitHub".
# Optional for local dev (login will not work without them).
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=your_github_client_id
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=<redacted>

# Zcash address the backend pays bounties FROM via z_sendmany.
# Optional for local dev (payouts only).
ADMIN_WALLET_ADDRESS=your_admin_zcash_address

# Runtime environment. Optional for local dev (defaults to development
# behavior: dev email override active, verbose prisma logs).
NODE_ENV=development
```

Notes:
- `USER` and `BACKEND_URL` appeared in older docs but are not read by the
  code; they have been removed. Do not set them.
- Zcash payments additionally require Zebrad and Zaino installed and
  running; see https://zechub.wiki/developers. That setup is out of scope
  for a basic local run.
